\section{Purpose}{

\code{trial_end_details} determines the realized trial end time on the
calendar scale. This is the time at which administrative follow-up stops and
final analysis is assumed to occur.

It works together with:
\itemize{
\item \code{enrollment_details}, which determines when each subject enters
the trial, and
\item \code{followup_details}, which determines subject-level follow-up
limits once the trial end time is known.
}

These trial-calendar features can be used with continuous, binary, count,
or time-to-event endpoints. For non-TTE endpoints, the main effect is on the
returned calendar quantities such as \code{enrollTime},
\code{availableFollowup}, and \code{sim$meta$trial_calendar}.

For time-to-event endpoints, enrollment times and event times also combine
to form calendar event times:
\deqn{
  \mathrm{calendar\ event\ time}_i = T_{E,i} + T_i,
}
where \eqn{T_{E,i}} is enrollment time and \eqn{T_i} is subject-level
follow-up time to event or censoring.
}

